# M7.3 acceptance: first run and the chat pane's action for each error kind,
# against a fake sidecar (no Claude calls, no network).
#
# Run from the worktree root. The app runs from a copy next to the fake
# sidecar, installed as `reader-sidecar`, so SidecarClient finds it the way a
# packaged app finds its sidecar, and deleting that file later makes a
# restart fail. READER_SIDECAR_CMD must not be set (it would win over the
# file and the restart could never fail):
#
#   H=$(mktemp -d)
#   O=<repo>/.verify/m7.3/<impl|review|tester>
#   mkdir -p "$H/bin"
#   cp build/app/agentic-reader "$H/bin/agentic-reader"
#   cp tests/acceptance/m7.3-fake-sidecar.sh "$H/bin/reader-sidecar"
#   chmod +x "$H/bin/reader-sidecar"
#   env -u READER_SIDECAR_CMD READER_FAKE_LOG="$H/fake.log" \
#     scripts/shot.sh -o "$O" -s tests/acceptance/m7.3.steps -- \
#     env HOME="$H" DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/nonexistent \
#     "$H/bin/agentic-reader" "$PWD/tests/data/sample.pdf"
#   grep -c '^start key=unset$' "$H/fake.log"             # must print 4
#   grep -c '^start key=set$' "$H/fake.log"               # must print 1
#   grep -c '^prompt Please RATELIMIT me$' "$H/fake.log"  # must print 2
#   test ! -e "$H/bin/reader-sidecar"                      # must succeed
#
# Pass: shot.sh exits 0, every shot matches its comment, and the four checks
# behave as stated:
#   - 4 main sidecar launches: at start, after the first-run save, after the
#     save from the auth banner, and the automatic restart after the crash.
#     OK with nothing changed starts none (M7.2 carried note), and the last
#     save starts none because the sidecar file is gone.
#   - 1 Test key sidecar (it got the typed key).
#   - "Please RATELIMIT me" reached the sidecar twice: the prompt and Retry.
#   - UNINSTALL removed the copied sidecar.
#
# How first run is reached: the scratch HOME has no config file, so the
# developer login is off (its default), and the unreachable session bus makes
# the key store unavailable, so no key is stored. That is "no key and dev mode
# off" (spec item 1). Enabling "Use my local Claude Code login (developer)" in
# Preferences is the only way out of first run in this container, since no key
# can be saved without a secret service.
#
# The fake sidecar (tests/acceptance/m7.3-fake-sidecar.sh, see its header)
# answers each prompt by an upper-case word in its text: AUTH, RATELIMIT
# (first time an error, then "Retry worked: <text>"), CLIMISSING, PROCESSFAIL,
# BUSY, INTERNAL, MYSTERY (an unknown kind), CRASH (the sidecar exits),
# UNINSTALL (deletes $H/bin/reader-sidecar). Other text gets "Echo: <text>".
# Every reply ends with a cost line for $0.0010, 10 in, 5 out tokens. Test key
# with a key containing SLOW gets no answer, and that sidecar lingers 10 s
# after its stdin closes.
#
# Assumptions (the spec is silent; the implementer conforms or files a
# TEST DISPUTE):
#   - Layout as in tests/acceptance/m5.2.steps: 1400x900 window at the
#     origin, chat pane x 980..1400, input at about (1180, 800), the button
#     row's bottom edge within 10 px of the status bar (y 876).
#   - SetupBanner (app/src/chat/SetupBanner.{h,cpp}) sits at the bottom of the
#     chat pane in place of the input and the Send/Stop row, under the message
#     view. Its "Open Settings" is a button, right-aligned in the banner's
#     bottom row with its bottom edge within 10 px of the status bar, so
#     (1355, 850) hits it, as it hits Stop when the input shows. The console
#     link is a hyperlink whose visible text is the URL
#     https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys (or that URL without
#     "https://"). The steps never click it (no browser here).
#   - The auth banner is the same SetupBanner with the text "API key
#     rejected", in the same place, with "Open Settings" in the same spot.
#   - "Open Settings" opens the same Preferences dialog as Edit > Preferences,
#     focus in the key field, Tab order as in m7.1.steps: key field, Show,
#     Test key, model field, dev check box. Return in the model field is OK.
#     Escape is Cancel.
#   - After Preferences closes with OK, the chat pane re-checks first run: the
#     banner (first-run or auth) goes away and the input comes back when a key
#     is stored or the developer login is on. Cancel changes nothing.
#   - rate_limit: the notice is inline in the message view. Its retry button
#     is a wxButton labelled "Retry" at the left end of the button row (left
#     edge within 10 px of the pane's left edge; Send and Stop stay
#     right-aligned), so (1030, 850) hits it. It shows only while the latest
#     reply ended with rate_limit. Pressing it sends the same prompt text
#     again; showing the user's message a second time is optional.
#   - process: the chat is reopened in the running sidecar (the existing
#     reopen path, M5.2 carried note), not by restarting the sidecar. The
#     input stays enabled.
#   - cli_missing: the chat is reopened the same way and the input stays
#     enabled. The message is shown inline (not as a banner).
#   - The sidecar itself exiting (EVT_SIDECAR_DOWN, "CRASH") ends the reply
#     with a notice that the agent stopped and is restarting. Either the
#     M5.2 wording ("The assistant stopped unexpectedly ... It is restarting")
#     or "Agent stopped, restarting…" passes.
#   - Wording that must appear verbatim (case-insensitive, "..." for "…"
#     passes): "Add your Anthropic API key to start", "Open Settings",
#     "API key rejected", "Installation is incomplete, reinstall the app",
#     "Agent stopped, restarting…". The sidecar's own message may follow
#     these, for example "Error: simulated internal failure".
#
# Carried notes covered here: KeyTester shutdown off the UI thread (shot
# settings-reopened-promptly), OK with no change restarts nothing (shot
# ok-without-changes and the start count), a failed restart after saving
# shows the unavailable state (shot restart-failed-unavailable).
# Not covered: a rejected RateLimitEvent followed by a non-error result
# reaches the app as a plain `result` (the protocol carries no rate-limit
# signal in that case), and a crash after an interrupt (the sidecar decides
# both; the app cannot see them). The double error box on a failed key store
# save needs a secret service that fails a save.
wait 3

# First run. Center pane: page 1 of sample.pdf. Chat pane: the message view
# on top, and at the bottom, where the input and Send/Stop were, a banner with
# the text "Add your Anthropic API key to start", a link reading
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys (blue or underlined), and an
# "Open Settings" button at its bottom right. No input field, no Send and no
# Stop button are visible. No red error text and no dialog.
shot first-run-banner

click 1355 850
wait 2

# "Open Settings" opened the Preferences dialog over the main window: the
# empty API key field with Show and Test key, the model field, and the
# unchecked "Use my local Claude Code login (developer)" check box, with OK
# and Cancel. (The red "cannot be stored securely" message is expected here.)
shot settings-from-banner

type sk-ant-test-SLOWKEY0123456789
key Tab Tab
key space
wait 1.5

# Test key is running: the dialog shows "Testing the key..." and the key
# field shows 29 mask characters. Nothing else changed.
shot key-test-running

key Escape
click 1355 850
wait 1

# Cancel during a running Test key does not freeze the app (M7.1 carried
# note: the test sidecar ignores stdin EOF for 10 s, so a shutdown on the UI
# thread blocks for 3 s). About 2 s after Escape the second click on "Open
# Settings" has already opened a fresh Preferences dialog: empty key field, no
# "Testing the key..." text, dev check box unchecked. The screen is fully
# painted (no grey or blank areas in the dialog or the main window).
shot settings-reopened-promptly

key Tab Tab Tab Tab
key space
wait 0.5

# The dev check box "Use my local Claude Code login (developer)" is checked.
shot dev-login-checked

key shift+Tab
key Return
wait 3

# The dialog is closed. The first-run banner is gone: the chat pane shows the
# message view with the grey line "Settings changed, sidecar restarted", and
# under it the empty input, Send (enabled) and Stop (greyed out), as in M5.2.
# No Retry button. The status bar reads "Assistant ready".
shot chat-ready

click 1180 800
type Hello there
key Return
wait 2.5

# A working chat: the user message "Hello there", the reply "Echo: Hello
# there" and under it the grey cost line ($0.0010, 10 in, 5 out). No red text.
# Send is enabled.
shot working-reply

key alt+e
wait 1
key p
wait 2
key Tab Tab Tab
key Return
wait 2

# OK with nothing changed restarted nothing (M7.2 carried note): the dialog
# is closed, the chat pane still ends with the "Echo: Hello there" reply and
# its cost line, with no second "Settings changed, sidecar restarted" line
# and no "Stopped." line. The status bar reads "Assistant ready".
shot ok-without-changes

click 1180 800
type Trigger AUTH now
key Return
wait 2.5

# auth: the user message "Trigger AUTH now" is in the view. The input and
# Send/Stop are replaced by the banner reading "API key rejected" with the
# "Open Settings" button at its bottom right. The first-run text "Add your
# Anthropic API key to start" is not shown.
shot auth-banner

click 1355 850
wait 2
key Tab Tab Tab
type claude-test-model
key Return
wait 3

# "Open Settings" on the auth banner opened Preferences (the model was set to
# claude-test-model and saved). The dialog is closed, the auth banner is
# gone, and the input with Send (enabled) and Stop is back. The view ends with
# the grey line "Settings changed, sidecar restarted". Status bar "Assistant
# ready".
shot auth-banner-cleared

click 1180 800
type Please RATELIMIT me
key Return
wait 2.5

# rate_limit: under the user message "Please RATELIMIT me" an inline notice in
# the message view says the rate limit was reached (for example "rate limit
# reached, try again later"). A "Retry" button shows at the left end of the
# button row, Send is enabled, the input is visible (no banner), and no cost
# line follows the notice.
shot rate-limit-notice

click 1030 850
wait 2.5

# Retry resent the prompt: the view now ends with the reply "Retry worked:
# Please RATELIMIT me" and its grey cost line. The Retry button is gone.
# Send is enabled.
shot rate-limit-retried

click 1180 800
type Trigger INTERNAL now
key Return
wait 2
click 1180 800
type Trigger MYSTERY now
key Return
wait 2

# Other kinds are inline: under "Trigger INTERNAL now" an inline red message
# containing "simulated internal failure", and under "Trigger MYSTERY now" an
# inline red message containing "simulated unknown failure". No banner, no
# Retry button, no dialog. The input is visible and Send is enabled.
shot inline-errors

click 1180 800
type Trigger BUSY now
key Return
wait 3.5

# busy is ignored: under "Trigger BUSY now" the whole reply "Working on it.
# Still working, done." and its grey cost line. No notice of any kind (no
# "busy", no red text) and no Retry button. Send is enabled.
shot busy-ignored

click 1180 800
type Trigger PROCESSFAIL now
key Return
wait 2

# process: under "Trigger PROCESSFAIL now" the notice "Agent stopped,
# restarting…" (or "..."). No banner, no dialog. The input is visible and
# Send is enabled.
shot process-restarting

click 1180 800
type After the process error
key Return
wait 2.5

# The chat was reopened after the process error: "After the process error"
# got the reply "Echo: After the process error" and its cost line. No red
# "chat is not open" notice.
shot after-process

click 1180 800
type Trigger CRASH now
key Return
wait 4

# The sidecar itself exited: under "Trigger CRASH now" the partial reply
# "About to crash." and a notice that the agent stopped and is restarting.
# The restarted sidecar is up: the status bar reads "Assistant ready" and
# Send is enabled.
shot sidecar-crash

click 1180 800
type After the crash
key Return
wait 2.5

# The chat works after the restart: "After the crash" got the reply "Echo:
# After the crash" and its cost line. No red text after the crash notice.
shot after-crash

click 1180 800
type Trigger CLIMISSING now
key Return
wait 2

# cli_missing: under "Trigger CLIMISSING now" the message "Installation is
# incomplete, reinstall the app", inline in the view (no banner, no dialog).
# The input is still visible.
shot cli-missing

click 1180 800
type UNINSTALL the sidecar
key Return
wait 2.5

# The reply reads "Removed reader-sidecar." (the copied sidecar file is gone).
# "Not removed: ..." means the run did not follow the header and the next
# shot is meaningless.
shot sidecar-removed

key alt+e
wait 1
key p
wait 2
key Tab Tab Tab
type claude-other-model
key Return
wait 3

# The restart after saving failed because the sidecar file is gone (M7.2
# carried note): the dialog is closed, the status bar reads "Assistant
# unavailable" (followed by a reason), not "Assistant ready" and not
# "Settings changed, sidecar restarted". The chat pane ends with a red notice
# that the assistant is unavailable, and Send is greyed out.
shot restart-failed-unavailable
